1
00:04:11,428 --> 00:04:17,428
As belles, they were ding-dongs... they enlisted, and were rotten to the corps... and when
things got hotter... they went to the cooler... now, they're on the loose again!

2
00:08:22,857 --> 00:08:28,857
The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again is a comedy, family,
western film directed by Vincent McEveety.

3
00:12:34,285 --> 00:12:40,285
Amos and Theodore, the two bumbling outlaw wannabes from The Apple
Dumpling Gang, are back and trying to make it on their own.

4
00:16:45,714 --> 00:16:51,714
This time, the crazy duo gets involved in an army supply theft case --
and, of course, gets in lots of comic trouble along the way!

5
00:20:57,142 --> 00:21:03,142
Amos Tucker, played by Tim Conway.

6
00:25:08,571 --> 00:25:14,571
Theodore, played by Don Knotts.

7
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Jeff Reed, played by Tim Matheson.

8
00:33:31,428 --> 00:33:37,428
Woolly Bill Hitchcock, played by Kenneth Mars.

9
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Miss Millie Gaskill, played by Elyssa Davalos.

10
00:41:54,285 --> 00:42:00,285
Big Mac, played by Jack Elam.

11
00:46:05,714 --> 00:46:11,714
The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American
comedy-Western film directed by Norman Tokar.

12
00:50:17,142 --> 00:50:23,142
It follows a slick gambler named Russell Donovan (Bill Bixby) who is duped
into taking care of three orphans who eventually strike gold.

13
00:54:28,571 --> 00:54:34,571
It was produced by Walt Disney Productions.

14
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
The film is based on the 1971 novel of the same name by Jack M.

15
01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:57,428
Don Tait wrote the screenplay.

16
01:07:02,857 --> 01:07:08,857
The so-called "Apple Dumpling Gang" are named after their
favorite American dessert treat, the apple dumpling.

17
01:11:14,285 --> 01:11:20,285
It is also known as being the first film to feature the
comedy duo of Don Knotts and Tim Conway.

18
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
Buddy Baker composed the music for the film and its sequel, The Apple Dumpling
Gang Rides Again, with Joseph Dubin performing the orchestration.

19
01:19:37,142 --> 01:19:43,142
The song "The Apple Dumpling Gang", as heard in the opening and closing credits, was composed
by Shane Tatum and was performed by Randy Sparks and the Back Porch Majority.

20
01:23:48,571 --> 01:23:54,571
The tone is lighthearted.
